#. Tag: title
#: usage.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kpilot; Data Viewers and Main Window Interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter describes the usage of &kpilot;'s main window; as a viewer "
"application for data on the &handheld;, and its menu structure. The main "
"window of &kpilot; also contains the &HotSync;-log, which can be useful when "
"debugging problems."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kpilot; starts up with a splash screen, and then switches to showing the "
"&HotSync;-log, as shown <link linkend=\"main-app\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: usage.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The Main Window</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: usage.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpilot; Main Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: usage.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Main Window</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The Main Window</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "The main window contains the application menu, which we will deal with here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenu>file</guimenu> menu contains the synchronization menu items. "
"Note that these items do not start the sync process, they only select what "
"the new sync will be. To really start it, you must press the HotSync button "
"on your &PalmPilot;'s cradle (or on the &handheld; itself, when there is no "
"cradle)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid "It is not possible to cancel a sync operation once the request has been made."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information regarding the synchronization functionality, please "
"check the <link linkend=\"synchronization\">Synchronization Chapter</link> "
"of this handbook, where you can find detailed descriptions of the "
"synchronization methods and options offered by &kpilot;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>HotSync</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Make the next sync a &HotSync;. For more information, please check the <link "
"linkend=\"sync-s\"> Syncing your &handheld; data</link> section of this "
"handbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>FastSync</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(not available with all installations) Make the next sync a FastSync. For "
"more information, please check the <link linkend=\"sync-s\">Syncing your "
"&handheld; data</link> section of this handbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>FullSync</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(not available with all installations) Make the next sync a FullSync. For "
"more information, please check the <link linkend=\"sync-s\"> Syncing your "
"&handheld; data</link> section of this handbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Backup</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Make the next sync a full backup of your &PalmPilot; data. This action can "
"take several minutes. For more information, please check the <link linkend="
"\"backup\"> Backing up your &handheld; data</link> section of this handbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first thing you should do after starting &kpilot; for the first time is "
"make a full backup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Restore</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This copies all the data from a previous backup on your <acronym>PC</"
"acronym> to your &PalmPilot;, replacing whatever data was there. Use this if "
"your &PalmPilot; suffers some from software or hardware failure (or is "
"replaced by a new one). For more information, please check the <link linkend="
"\"restore\"> Restoring your &handheld; data</link> section of this handbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Doing a restore will erase all data on the &PalmPilot; before restoring the "
"information from your <acronym>PC</acronym>!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Copy Handheld to PC</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This runs all conduits and syncs all databases, but instead of merging the "
"information from both sources, it will copy the handheld data to the PC. "
"<emphasis>Use with care, as this option erases the changes you made in your "
"PC since the last sync</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Copy PC to Handheld</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This runs all conduits and syncs all databases, but instead of merging the "
"information from both sources, it will copy the PC data to the handheld. "
"<emphasis>Use with care, as this option erases the changes you made in your "
"handheld since the last sync</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Quit</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Quits &kpilot;, closing the main window and stopping the daemon if that "
"<link linkend=\"stopdaemononexit\">configuration option</link> is enabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> menu allows you to configure &kpilot; main "
"interface and fine-tune the synchronization process with the &handheld;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Statusbar</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click this menu item to toggle &kpilot;'s status bar on and off, or in other "
"words, to show it if hidden, or to hide it if shown."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Toolbar</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click this menu item to toggle &kpilot;'s toolbar on and off, or in other "
"words, to show it if hidden, or to hide it if shown."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Shortcuts...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Displays &kpilot;'s shortcut configuration dialog, allowing you change or "
"create key bindings, which are associations between actions (for example, "
"opening &kpilot;'s configuration dialog) and keys or key combinations (for "
"instance, Ctrl + Shift + a)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:279
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Toolbars...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:285
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Displays &kpilot;'s toolbar configuration dialog. This dialog lists all "
"actions available for use on the toolbar, and the actions currently "
"displayed, allowing you to add or remove actions, and move the actions which "
"already are on the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure KPilot...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:303
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Displays &kpilot;'s configuration dialog, allowing you to match your "
"hardware with the configuration, so that &kpilot; can talk with your "
"&handheld;, to configure the way &kpilot; synchronizes your &PalmPilot; with "
"your desktop applications (through conduits) and the way it shows the data "
"from your &PalmPilot; in the <link linkend=\"builtin\">built-in viewers</"
"link>. The <link linkend=\"configure\"> Configuring &kpilot;</link> chapter "
"of this handbook offers detailed information about these configuration "
"options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: usage.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configuration Wizard...</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Displays &kpilot;'s configuration wizard dialog. The <link linkend="
"\"configwizard\">configuration wizard</link> helps you to set up &kpilot; to "
"communicate with the &PalmPilot; and to configure the conduits as a group. "
"It's a great start for new users, and you can always fine-tune your "
"preferences later, using the <link linkend=\"configure\">configure dialog</"
"link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: usage.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid "Built-in Applications"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:345
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To select one of the Built in applications, just click its icon on "
"&kpilot;'s sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: usage.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>KPilot's Sidebar</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: usage.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>KPilot's Sidebar</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>KPilot's Sidebar</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selecting one of the built-in applications will cause that application to "
"appear in &kpilot;'s main window. You may use the viewer applications to "
"edit the information, by enabling this option in the <link linkend=\"page-"
"viewers\">database viewer's configuration dialog</link>. The ability to view "
"and edit private records is configurable too."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Any changes you make to the &PalmPilot; databases with the built-in "
"applications (such as deleting a memo) do not take effect on the &PalmPilot; "
"until the next HotSync."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the <guilabel>Make internal viewers editable</guilabel> option is not "
"enabled, the changes in the viewers are not synchronized with your "
"&handheld;, and will be lost. In recent versions of &kpilot; it is not "
"possible enable this option, and therefore, to edit the databases with the "
"viewers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: usage.docbook:384
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Todo Viewer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The todo application allows you to view the tasks from your &PalmPilot;, add "
"new tasks and edit or delete existing ones. The changes you made are applied "
"to the &handheld; the next time you &HotSync;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: usage.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid "Todo Viewer Application"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: usage.docbook:396
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Todo Viewer Application</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The Todo Viewer Application</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:401
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The todo application has a drop down box for the memo categories defined in "
"the &PalmPilot;. In the screenshot, category <quote>All</quote> is selected. "
"Underneath the drop down box is a list of todo entries, with a check box "
"indicating if they are completed or not. You can click the check box to "
"toggle the todo item between completed and not completed status. Clicking on "
"one of the todo items in the list will display its details in the text box "
"labelled <guilabel>Todo info:</guilabel> to the right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have the <guilabel>Make internal viewers editable</guilabel> option "
"enabled in the <link linkend=\"page-viewers\">viewers configuration page</"
"link> you can use the buttons <guibutton>Edit Record...</guibutton>, "
"<guibutton>New Record...</guibutton> and <guibutton>Delete Record</"
"guibutton> to edit the todo data from your &handheld;, and sync the data in "
"the next &HotSync;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Edit Record...</guibutton> button opens a dialog where you "
"can edit the details of the currently selected todo item, including "
"description, priority and end date. Click the <guibutton>New Record...</"
"guibutton> button to open the same dialog, but instead of editing the "
"current selected record, a new todo will be added to the list. And finally, "
"click the <guibutton>Delete Record</guibutton> button to remove the selected "
"todo record from the list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: usage.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Address Viewer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The address viewer lets you view, create, delete and edit addresses from the "
"&PalmPilot;, and synchronize changes back. The addresses can be sorted and "
"viewed in the <guilabel>\"Last, first\"</guilabel> or <guilabel>\"Company, "
"last\"</guilabel> format, depending on your <link linkend=\"page-viewers"
"\">viewers configuration.</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: usage.docbook:454
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The Address Viewer Application</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: usage.docbook:457
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Address Viewer Application</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:458
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The Address Viewer Application</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:463
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The address application resembles the todo application; the drop down box, "
"buttons, list and text area function exactly the same, allowing you to "
"select, view and edit an address as on the &PalmPilot;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Edit Record...</guibutton> dialog allows you to edit the "
"<guilabel>Last Name</guilabel>, <guilabel>First Name</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Company</guilabel>, &etc; fields, just as if you where using your "
"&handheld;. Click the <guibutton>New Record...</guibutton> button to open "
"the same dialog, but instead of editing the current selected record, a new "
"address will be added to the list. Click the <guibutton>Delete Record</"
"guibutton> button to remove the selected address from the list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: usage.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Memo Viewer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The memo application allows you to view the memos on your &PalmPilot;, "
"export them to text files, import new ones to be installed the next time you "
"&HotSync;, or edit existing ones."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: usage.docbook:506
#, no-c-format
msgid "Memo Viewer Application"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: usage.docbook:509
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Memo Viewer Application</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:510
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The Memo Viewer Application</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:514
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The memo application has a drop down box for the memo categories defined in "
"the &PalmPilot;. Here category <quote>All</quote> is selected. Underneath "
"the drop down box is a list of memo titles. These are the first lines of the "
"memos, just like in the &PalmPilot; memo application. Clicking on one of the "
"memo titles in the list box will display it in the text box labelled "
"<guilabel>Memo Text:</guilabel> to the right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:526
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When a memo is selected, you can use the buttons <guibutton>Export Memo...</"
"guibutton> and <guibutton>Delete Memo</guibutton> to export the selected "
"memo to a file or to delete the selected memo. Exporting a memo requires you "
"to give a filename; the memo is written to that file. Take care not to "
"overwrite existing files with this action. Deleting a memo does not affect "
"the &PalmPilot; until the next &HotSync;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:540
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Import Memo...</guibutton> button allows you to read a text "
"file and add it &mdash; as a memo &mdash; to the &PalmPilot;. Importing a "
"memo does not take effect until the next &HotSync;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: usage.docbook:565
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The Generic DB Viewer</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:567
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In short, databases are all files stored in your &handheld;. A database can "
"be either a record database, which stores dynamic information created by the "
"user (for instance, the addresses or the todo information), or a resource "
"database, which tend to be static (for instance the applications)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:574
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Generic DB Viewer is a tool to view and analyze databases stored on your "
"handheld, especially record databases. It helps a lot creating new conduits "
"and to debug existing ones."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:579
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While it is possible use the database viewer to edit, add and delete "
"records, you should really know what you are doing, otherwise you may damage "
"your data. Use the viewer applications or conduits to edit your &handheld; "
"data instead, in a normal usage scenario."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: usage.docbook:591
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The Generic DB Viewer</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: usage.docbook:594
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Generic DB Viewer</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:595
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The Generic DB Viewer</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: usage.docbook:603
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The File Installer</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:604
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Just hit the <guibutton>Add File...</guibutton> button to add a file to the "
"<guilabel>Files to Install:</guilabel> list. These files will be installed "
"on your &PalmPilot; during the next &HotSync; if <guilabel>Sync Files</"
"guilabel> is checked in the conduits section of the <link linkend=\"configure"
"\">configuration dialog</link>. If you choose not to install these files on "
"the &PalmPilot;, just hit <guibutton>Clear List</guibutton> to remove any "
"pending files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:618
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are using the &HotSync; Daemon you may drag and drop files or &URL;s "
"onto the docked icon on the toolbar. The file installer application also "
"supports dragging and dropping into the <guilabel>Files to Install:</"
"guilabel>area. Provided <guilabel>Sync Files</guilabel> is checked in the "
"<link linkend=\"page-general\">settings dialog</link> they will be installed "
"the next time you HotSync."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:629
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An internal copy of the file is kept, so you can even drag and drop &URL;s "
"from &konqueror;!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: usage.docbook:636
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The File Installer</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: usage.docbook:639
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The File Installer</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: usage.docbook:640
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The File Installer</para>"
msgstr ""

